# Contract

What @REPO@ promises, what it needs, and the rules a caller follows.

The library inherits the [Kokeb Labs library contract](https://github.com/kokeb-labs/.github/blob/main/standards/library.md);
this page states only what is specific to it.

## Promises

- Every fallible call returns `Result<T>`; nothing throws.
- Every call returns `Error::NotInitialized` before `Initialize()` succeeds.
- An invalid argument changes nothing and returns `Error::InvalidArgument`.
- One include root, `@ROOT@/`; no macro leaks out of a public header.

## Depends on

| Dependency | Version | Why |
| --- | --- | --- |
| A C++20 compiler | GCC 10, Clang 13 or later | |
| CMake | 3.16 or later | Generates `@ROOT@/Version.h` |

Nothing else: no RTOS, no SDK, no other repository of the org.

## Threading

No object is thread-safe and none takes a lock. Use each object from one task at a time, or guard it with one
mutex. The calls do not block and allocate nothing, so they may run in an ISR.

## Errors

| `Error` | Value | Returned when |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `Ok` | 0 | The call succeeded |
| `NotInitialized` | 1 | `Initialize()` has not succeeded, or `Deinitialize()` ran since |
| `InvalidArgument` | 2 | A window outside 1 to the capacity, a negative limit, a NaN or rejected sample |
| `Empty` | 16 | `Average()` before the first sample |

Above the library, map them to the caller's status type once: `Empty` to `NotFound` or `Busy`, as fits the caller.

## Memory

No heap. A `MovingAverage<N>` holds `N` floats plus about 24 bytes.

## Platform

Platform-free: the same code on any target with a C++20 compiler, including the host tests.

## Deviations from the standard

None.
